        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=COMPANY :  {{ $json.company_name }}\nPlan : {{ $json.plan }}\nDays since last login : {{ $json.days_since_login }}\nFeature Usage : {{ $json.feature_usage_pct }}\nSupport Tickets : {{ $json.support_tickets_30d }}\nPayment status : {{ $json.payment_status }}\nRisk tier :{{ $json.risk_tier }}",
        "options": {
          "systemMessage": "You are writing short warm retention email for a SaaS Customers at risk of churning , Reference their specific situation naturally \nDon't sound like a template.\nKeep it under 120 words. offer a clean next step( reply to this email, or book a call or check out a specific feature). \nNever mention \"risk score\" or internal metrices to the Customers.\nwrite email using company name as a first name always\nGIVE OUTPUT STRICTLY IN JSON FORMAT WITH SUBJECT AND BODY SEPARATELY.\nWrite a short, warm retention email for a business customer. You do NOT have a contact's first name — only the company name. Address the email using the company name (e.g., \"Hi team at {{company_name}}\" or \"Hi {{company_name}} team\") — never invent or assume a first name. Reference their specific situation naturally. Keep it under 120 words. Offer a clear next step."
        }
